{"slug":"southbank","label":"SOUTHBANK","colour":"#A1E0FF","items":[{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","jobtitle":"Former member of the office, architect","recorded":"2014-11-05","hls":"https://customer-syg1o9n270h63juf.cloudflarestream.com/58b2726a1ed4f5da4e700326d969a595/manifest/video.m3u8","start":484,"end":622,"topicId":"southbank","segments":[{"start":484,"end":622,"topicId":"southbank"}],"cards":[{"time":485,"title":"South Bank","id":"south-bank"},{"time":488.52,"title":"Tony Banks","id":"tony-banks"},{"time":492.2,"title":"GLC","id":"glc"},{"time":577,"title":"London Eye","id":"london-eye"}]}],"cards":{"GLC":{"slug":"glc","body":"<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The Greater London Council (GLC) was the top-tier <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_government\">local government</a> administrative body for <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_London\">Greater London</a> from 1965 to 1986. It replaced the earlier <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_County_Council\">London County Council</a> (LCC) which had covered a much smaller area. The GLC was dissolved in 1986 by the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_Government_Act_1985\">Local Government Act 1985</a> and its powers were devolved to the London boroughs and other entities.</p>","subtitle":"Greater London Council","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/glc.jpg","external":"http://news.bbc.co.uk/onthisday/hi/dates/stories/march/31/newsid_2530000/2530803.stm","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/London,+UK/@51.5073509,-0.1277583,7z","also":[{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":205.2,"topicId":"building","topicLabel":"Building"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":492.2,"topicId":"southbank","topicLabel":"SOUTHBANK"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":143,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1549.2,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]},"London Eye":{"slug":"london-eye","body":"The London Eye is a giant <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferris_wheel\">Ferris wheel</a> on the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Bank\">South Bank</a> of the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Thames\">River Thames</a> in <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London\">London</a>. Also known as the Millennium Wheel, its official name was originally the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Airways\">British Airways</a> London Eye, then the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merlin_Entertainments\">Merlin Entertainments</a> London Eye, between January 2011 and August 2014, the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EDF_Energy\">EDF Energy</a> London Eye and is now called The London Eye.\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.0pt; mso-pagination: none; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"></p>","subtitle":"Ferris Wheel","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/london-eye.jpg","external":"http://www.londoneye.com","location":"https://maps.google.com/?q=london+eye","also":[{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":577,"topicId":"southbank","topicLabel":"SOUTHBANK"}]},"South Bank":{"slug":"south-bank","body":"In 1984 Price proposed the redevelopment of London's <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Bank\">South Bank</a>, and foresaw the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Eye\">London Eye</a> by suggesting that a giant <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferris_wheel\">Ferris wheel</a> should be constructed by the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Thames\">River Thames</a>.\r\n\r\n“A city should be sufficiently old, rich and well-serviced to be able to accommodate a vast range of disparate, peculiar, incomparable objects, space, activities and people. The resultant mix, to be both convivial and convenient, is achieved through constant change in community appetites and individual mores – and not through a Band-Aid of architectural ingenuity trying to be all things to all men…”\r\n\r\n(Price Probes, BD, 16 September 1994)<!--more-->","subtitle":"Job no. 159","image":null,"external":"http://www.aaschool.ac.uk/PUBLIC/AAPUBLICATIONS/aboutpublications\n.php","location":"https://maps.google.com/?q=london+eye","also":[{"slug":"carlos-villanueva-brandt","name":"Carlos Villanueva Brandt","time":20.56,"topicId":"institutions","topicLabel":"Institutions"},{"slug":"carlos-villanueva-brandt","name":"Carlos Villanueva Brandt","time":837.4,"topicId":"enabling","topicLabel":"Enabling"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":203.56,"topicId":"building","topicLabel":"Building"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":485,"topicId":"southbank","topicLabel":"SOUTHBANK"}]},"Tony Banks":{"slug":"tony-banks","body":"<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Anthony Louis Banks, Baron Stratford (8 April 1942 – 8 January 2006) was a British <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labour_Party_(UK)\">Labour Party</a> politician, who was a member of parliament (MP) from <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom_general_election,_1983\">1983</a> to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom_general_election,_2005\">2005</a>, before being made a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peerage_(disambiguation)\">Member</a> of the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Lords\">House of Lords</a>. In <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_the_United_Kingdom\">government</a>, he served for two years as <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_for_Culture,_Media_and_Sport\">Minister for Sport</a>. He was well known in the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Commons_of_the_United_Kingdom\">House of Commons</a> for his acid tongue.</p>","subtitle":"Politician","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/tony-banks.jpg","external":"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Banks,_Baron_Stratford","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/London,+UK/@51.5073509,-0.1277583,7z","also":[{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":488.52,"topicId":"southbank","topicLabel":"SOUTHBANK"}]}}}